{
  "name": "grass-snake",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/snakes.py): the GRASS SNAKE, Natrix natrix, a metre long and 2.7 cm thick, the tail a fifth of it tapering whip-thin; a distinct oval head, flat on top, with the big crown shields (frontal, parietals, supraoculars), round pupils in a golden iris; olive-grey above with black bars down each flank and small black spots in two rows on the back; the COLLAR -- two yellow half-moons behind the head, black ones behind them; white lips barred black; the belly pale chequered black. Coats: olive, grey, barred (N. helvetica), melanistic (no collar). It slithers on its seven segments.",
  "kind": "parts",
  "flags": {"print": "none"},
